       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Dose as written:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The labeled maximum for metformin is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given as no more than 850 mg per dose. Extended-release is capped at 2,000\u20132,500 mg/day. This order is about twice that.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,700 mg/day total, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and whether it's immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter it right away."
