       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A confirmation doesn't change my concern. 1,700 mg three times daily (5,100 mg/day) is twice the maximum daily dose, and a single 1,700 mg dose is twice the maximum per-dose amount. Nothing in the patient details you gave, such as normal renal and hepatic function, would justify it. The main risk is serious harm from metformin-associated lactic acidosis.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If the dose was a slip:** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any lower regimen you choose, right away.\n- **If you have a specific reason for the higher dose:** Please discuss it with the pharmacist or your attending first. If they approve, the order will need to go through whatever override process your hospital requires. I can include a note on the order documenting that.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
